#     actually stops a sale. The API changed `bookable` to be false only when
#     something gates — an operator LIVE with three listings selling was being
#     told "you cannot be booked yet" over a missing logo — and this portal
#     was gating the whole outstanding list on `!bookable`, so the change made
#     the list vanish. The list is now gated on `blocking` being non-empty,
#     which is what the field description asks for, and `gates` separates what
#     stops a sale from what is merely owed.
#
# NOT consumed here, and each needs its own change:
#   - nothing outstanding.
#
# The traveller document is byte-identical between this ref and the one
# yuvoy-app pins, so both frontends are back on ONE commit — the intent stated
# at the top of this file, which had drifted by two commits.
#
# `git ls-remote` was the check for this ref, not `gh api .../commits/master`,
